# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER COMMIT. This list is the project's non-negotiable git hygiene rule and
# is verified by `make check-clean` before the first push.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json

# --- Model weights and adapters --------------------------------------------
# Adapters live on the HF Hub and are referenced from the repo, never stored
# in it. A LoRA adapter is small enough to tempt you; do not.
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.gguf
*.onnx
adapter_model.*
adapter_config.json
checkpoints/
outputs/
runs/
# Training output root. Adapters and checkpoints live here and must never be
# committed - they are model weights. The adapter goes to the HF Hub and is
# referenced from the repo. The large-file pre-commit hook caught this once;
# the ignore rule is the durable fix.
out/

# --- Corpus and datasets ---------------------------------------------------
# Raw OpenStax PDFs are CC BY but large; they are fetched and checksummed by
# ragft.corpus.download instead. Generated QA goes to the HF Hub.
data/**
!data/MANIFEST.md
!data/.gitkeep
# Two small files under data/ ARE committed, because they are evidence rather
# than data. git needs the parent dirs un-ignored to reach them.
#   manifest.json  SHA-256 + source URLs + licences for every ingested PDF.
#   splits.json    Which section went to which split. This IS the
#                  decontamination guarantee - without it, "no training pair
#                  shares a passage with an eval question" is unverifiable.
!data/raw/
!data/raw/manifest.json
!data/corpus/
!data/corpus/splits.json
# The EVALUATION SET and the human labels. These are committed for the same
# reason as splits.json - they are evidence, not bulk data - and the case is
# stronger:
#
#   gold.jsonl              configs/eval/frozen.lock HASHES this file. Without
#                           it the freeze is unverifiable by anyone else: a
#                           clean checkout fails the harness check with
#                           "removed data/eval/gold.jsonl", which is exactly
#                           what an end-to-end reproduction hit. 300 items,
#                           human-verified in full, 190 KB.
#   gold_unanswerable.jsonl The hand-written abstention stratum. Cannot be
#                           regenerated - an LLM asked for unanswerable
#                           questions produces obviously out-of-domain ones.
#   human_judge_labels.jsonl The 100 labels behind Cohen's kappa = 0.452. The
#                           number that demoted the LLM judge to secondary is
#                           not checkable without them.
#
# None of these can be regenerated: they are human work product. Omitting them
# makes every eval number in this repo unreproducible by a third party.
!data/eval/
!data/eval/gold.jsonl
!data/eval/gold_unanswerable.jsonl
!data/eval/human_judge_labels.jsonl
*.pdf

# --- Experiment tracking / job output --------------------------------------
wandb/
*.log
logs/
slurm-*.out
nohup.out
.tmux-logs/

# --- Caches ----------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.cache/
.llm_cache/

# --- Vector store ----------------------------------------------------------
qdrant_storage/
data/index/

# --- Editor / OS -----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# --- Agent tooling scratch (not part of the project) ------------------------
.claude-flow/
